# RTSP low latency (highest priority)

Low-latency RTSP/live playback is the most important feature of upPlayer. Prefer it over convenience, overlays, or secondary UX when they conflict.

## Requirements

- Match CLI `mpv --profile=low-latency --untimed <rtsp>` end-to-end latency.
- UI has one **low-latency** switch; it always enables both `--profile=low-latency` and `--untimed` together.
- Live mode must spawn **mpv.exe** with those flags and the **URL on argv** (not idle + IPC `loadfile`).
- Do **not** add “clever” demuxer knobs (`demuxer-thread=no`, tiny `demuxer-max-bytes`, etc.): they stall the reader and fill the OS TCP buffer (~10s behind CLI).
- IPC `apply-profile` after lavf opens is too late; prefer exe backend over libmpv for live RTSP.
- Network URLs (`rtsp://`, `rtsps://`, `rtmp://`, etc.) should enter live mode automatically.

## When changing player code

- Side-by-side test against CLI mpv on the same RTSP URL.
- Do not regress live URL-on-cmdline spawn for unrelated features.
